    "step": "step:50-1",
    "summary": "Splits the phase `scrum: regroup and chasers` into nine laps with `laps::split`, so the merge's `bench-inspect` run shows where regroup's ~57 ms at 25k goes: `scrum: regroup: regroupers`, `faced`, `crowd`, `walk-back`, `trade-in`, then `scrum: chase: chasing`, `lookups`, `crowd` and `steer` (the last ends the phase with `lap`). `walk-back` and `trade-in` add up over the squads. Every part is timed on every tick, even with no squad to regroup or chase, so the parts always come in the same order. That meant dropping two `is_empty` guards around calls that already do nothing when their list is empty.",
    "title": "feat(native): time regroup and the chase in sub-laps"
  },
